{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"3355463585a5c5413b8958a56dc4d325b370b50e1e9785c1ee1a48ab08596740","digest":{"component_or_area":"op-cert documentation and ADR","key_entities":["docs/adr/NNNN-opcert-asymmetric.md","docs/migrations/hmac-opcert-removal.md",".opcert-key",".rebar/trusted_environments.yaml","ADR 0046","rebar.opcert.v1","verify.require_environment","verify.opcert_enforce_since","verify.opcert_remote_url"],"problem_keywords":["documentation","architecture decision record","operation certificate","asymmetric signing","environment attribution","security posture","producer signing","HMAC removal","migration"],"propositions":["An ADR documenting the operation-certificate asymmetric model must be created, covering environment-attribution, security postures (L2 no-transparency-log and L4 single-environment/no-threshold), and the authoritative-state-fetch integrity requirement.","The ADR must document uniform producer signing with auto-generated Ed25519 keys at .opcert-key per environment, out-of-band trust-root pinning via .rebar/trusted_environments.yaml, and the trusted-server runtime architecture behind an API Gateway with async job API.","The ADR must cross-reference ADR 0046, explain the era-anchor resolution for anti-rollback enforcement, and document the stateless/read-only server posture with client-side envelope persistence.","HMAC removal migration path via expand-contract must be documented in docs/migrations/hmac-opcert-removal.md with consumer policy enforcement via verify.require_environment and verify.opcert_enforce_since.","The ADR must contain the exact strings rebar.opcert.v1, trusted_environments.yaml, and ADR 0046; a test must verify file existence, non-empty content, and presence of these strings."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785820414557955577,"uuid":"2e2220a1-3c41-44b7-a46b-19cc852e99b0"}